  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.6.0.0\n\t\t\t- New, backward compatible: two metric output switches in AuditAndMetricsConfigurations, the same pair audits already have. IsMetricsDatabaseLoggingEnabled chooses whether spans are written to storage through IAuditAndMetricStorageBroker; IsMetricsAppInsightsLoggingEnabled chooses whether they are published as telemetry through the ActivitySource. Both default to true, so a host that sets neither behaves exactly as on 0.5.0.\n\t\t\t- Both are only read while IsMetricsEnabled is true, which stays the master switch over every metric output.\n\t\t\t- With database logging off, AddMetricAsync returns the stamped span that would have been stored, and telemetry records that span. With both off, nothing is stored or recorded, and the Log paths hand nothing to the dispatcher.\n\t\t\t- No public signature, interface or storage port has changed, and audits and security audits are unchanged. No migration is needed.\n\t\t\t- Dependencies: Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration, Configuration.Abstractions, Configuration.Binder, DependencyInjection and Logging.Abstractions move to 10.0.15 (from 10.0.13 and 10.0.14). A host that references any Microsoft.Extensions package at a lower 10.0.x version must raise it to 10.0.15, or restore fails with NU1605 (package downgrade).\n\t\t\t- Upgrade guide: https://github.com/NHSISL/NHSOneLondon.AuditAndMetrics#upgrading-from-05x",
